Cold: GCC 4/4, EvoCC 4/4; queued requests observed, clients/delete complete.
Warm: GCC 3/3, EvoCC 3/3; completion deltas and pending writeback observed,
      fdatasync returns EIO after daemon death, clients/delete complete.
All four nonce-bound boot/shutdown predicates PASS. No stalled final tasks.
This rules out these basic single-device schedules as sufficient to reproduce
the old stall; it is not proof that all cancellation schedules are correct.
No compiler or kernel source was repaired. Multi-device/backing-file/timing
interactions and the actual original blocked path remain unclosed.

Validation: GCC14 static build and independent Clang19 object compilation with
-std=gnu11 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror. For the warm variant add
-DUBLK_WARM_LOOP=1. The init includes the existing selftest-init.c with
-DUBLK_DIAGNOSTIC_PROBE -I/harness. Existing selftest.py flight: hvf-host,
KUnit autorun off, explicit QEMU drift, diagnostic budget 120 + 60 seconds.
No new benchmark framework. Each initramfs is under 2 MiB, with snapshot-backed
I/O and no full disk copy. Kernel recovery was concurrently active; the final
cold/warm flights may also overlap. No timing or performance claim.

