Follow-up controls (same retained Images/disks, no compiler/kernel repair):

The running variant adds -DUBLK_RUNNING_KILL=1 to the warm-loop control. It
never SIGSTOPs the daemon, retaining completion-versus-exit concurrency.
All three modes have confirmed outstanding I/O on both Images: 6/6 PASS,
all clients/delete finish and both guests shut down. This alone does not
reproduce the original failure.
